    "body": "~So the primary solution is \"don't run integration tests on bare metal because we need to set up certain environments in the tests and can't guarantee much.\" Unfortunately, there's no (easy) way to make sure tests are being run in a docker container, so we're currently using `ignore` as a proxy for `docker-only`.~\r\n\r\nEDIT: It appears that this is being caused in normal tests, not just integration tests like I thought.\r\n\r\nSince multiple people are getting hit by this, it's pretty clear we need a stronger version of this message somewhere. What do y'all think would be a good place to put that? The best place would be in the tests themselves, but there's no way to force printing of messages from within the tests (you need the user to pass some flags for output to be shown)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
